1. Check Git Configuration
     git config --global --list 
    #Shows the global Git configuration settings.

2. Set Username
     git config --global user.name "name"
    #Sets the username for Git commits.

3. Set Email
     git config --global user.email "mail id"
   #Sets the email for Git commits.

Repository Commands
4. Initialize Git Repository
     git init  #creates a new local Git repository.

5. Clone Repository
     git clone <repository_url> (Copies an existing repository from GitHub to your local system.)
     # example : git clone https://github.com/user/repo.git

File Tracking Commands
6. Check Status
     git status #Shows changed, staged, and untracked files

7. Add File to Staging
     git add filename #Adds a specific file to the staging area.

     Add all files:
     git add .

8. Commit Changes
     git commit -m "added commit message" #Saves staged changes to the repository.

Remote Repository Commands
9. Push Code
     git push origin branchname #Pushes local commits to the remote repository.
    Example:
      git push origin main

10. Pull Latest Code
      git pull # Fetches and merges changes from the remote repository.

11. Fetch Changes
      git fetch #Downloads changes from remote but does not merge.

Branch Management
12. Switch Branch
     git checkout branchname #Moves to another branch.

13. New Branch and Switch
      git checkout -b branchname

14. Modern Way to Switch Branch
      git switch branchname

Stash Commands
15. Stash Changes
    git stash  #Temporarily saves uncommitted changes.

16. Apply Stash
     git stash pop

17. List Stashes
    git stash list

History and Comparison
18. View Commit History
    git log

19. Show Commit Details
    git show

20. Show File Differences
    git diff

Advanced Git Commands
21. Merge Branch
    git merge branchname #Merges another branch into the current branch.

22. Rebase Branch
    git rebase branchname #git rebase branchname

23. Reset Changes
    git reset #Undo commits or staging changes.

24. Cherry Pick Commit
    git cherry-pick commit_id #Applies a specific commit from another branch.

Remote Commands
25. Check Remote Repository
    git remote

26. Show Remote URL
    git remote -v
    #origin https://github.com/user/repo.git (fetch)
    #origin https://github.com/user/repo.git (push)
